{
  "dom_id": "step-e7416",
  "name": "Example: Computing Variance Given the Expected Value of a Random Variable and Its Square",
  "problem": "If $\\textrm E[X] = 4$ and $\\textrm E[X^2] = 21,$ then what is $\\textrm{Var}[X]?$",
  "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E[X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =21-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =21-16 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
